# What Vercel does NOT need to build this site.
#
# Written 14 Aug 2026, after a CLI deploy sat at "Uploading (0.0B/882.6MB)" and
# never finished. 882 MB is not this site — it is the repository's *history* and
# its raw materials. Vercel installs its own dependencies and runs its own build,
# so everything below is uploaded for nothing and, at this size, is the difference
# between a deploy that lands in a minute and one that never does.
#
#   .git          926 MB   every version of every photograph ever committed
#   node_modules  582 MB   Vercel runs its own `npm install`
#   .next         172 MB   Vercel runs its own `next build`
#   reference      77 MB   crawled source material, never shipped
#
# The site itself is `public/` at 46 MB plus the source, and that is all that
# should ever go up.
#
# **If a build starts failing on a missing file, look here first.** Excluding
# something the build needs fails loudly at build time, which is the good kind of
# wrong — but it will look like a code error rather than an ignore-file error.

.git
node_modules
.next

# Raw materials and working files — none of it is imported by the app.
reference
docs
.superpowers
Mahua-property-logos
Forest-illustrations

# The measurement rigs and the image pipeline. They generate committed artefacts
# (`lib/*-art.ts`, `lib/media-manifest.ts`, `public/media`) and are never run at
# build time — `package.json`'s build script is a bare `next build`.
scripts

# Test files. The suite runs here, not on Vercel.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
vitest.config.ts
vitest.setup.ts
